Task 9.7: Redesign navigation with grouped sections and icons

Summary:
- Implemented grouped navigation sections with collapsible headers
- Added Lucide icon support throughout navigation system
- Redesigned PageSidebar with section management and icon display
- Updated mobile navigation to use icon-based tabs
- Removed cryptic abbreviations (IdxSet, DLC, Notify, Apps)
- Maintained backward compatibility with isNavActive and buildBreadcrumbs

Files modified:
- app/src/lib/navigation.ts: Added icon field to NavigationItem, created NavigationSection type, reorganized NAV_ITEMS into grouped sections
- app/src/components/shell/PageSidebar.tsx: Added section collapse/expand functionality, icon display, and collapsible headers
- app/src/components/shell/PageLayout.tsx: Updated mobile navigation to use icons, added flattenNavItems helper
- app/src/components/shell/PageSidebar.test.tsx: Created comprehensive tests for grouped navigation
- app/src/lib/navigation.test.ts: Created tests for NavigationSection type and icon fields
- app/src/components/shell/page-layout.test.tsx: Updated tests for icon-based mobile nav
- app/src/lib/prowlarr-routes.test.ts: Updated to work with new NavigationSection[] structure

Why: The navigation system needed better organization and visual hierarchy. Grouping related items into sections with icons improves user experience by making the interface more intuitive and discoverable. Cryptic abbreviations were replaced with meaningful labels to reduce cognitive load.
